Call microphone capture: mark the AudioRecord privacy sensitive on Android 11+.

The call's microphone is captured by WebRtcAudioRecord, which builds its
AudioRecord itself in createAudioRecordOnMOrHigher(). Nothing in that path
set AudioRecord.Builder.setPrivacySensitive(), so on Android 11 (API 30) and
above a privileged assistant (hotword or voice-interaction service) could
still capture the microphone at the same time as a call, whatever the app
did around the factory.

With setPrivacySensitive(true) the platform refuses concurrent capture for
the whole life of that AudioRecord, regardless of audio source. The flag is
only added on SDK_INT >= R (30); below that the Builder method does not exist
and the behaviour is unchanged. No other Builder parameter changes (source,
format, buffer size), so latency and routing are as before.

Only the Builder path (API 23+) is touched. The pre-M constructor path is
left alone: it can only run on API < 23, where the flag does not exist.

Written against webrtc-sdk/webrtc @ ba469aa2093ba950066258ca0a59a6fbd1295582
(the pinned m150 revision); no other patch of the series touches this file.
Verified with `git apply --check` on that file at that commit.

